    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, region-validated `postcode` support for owners, keeping each piece in a small single-responsibility unit and reusing the existing city\u2192region table.\n\n**Domain / data**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional, `^[0-9]{4}$`), so the generated DTOs carry it and the response includes it.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` field, `@Column`, accessors, and a backstop `@Pattern` mirroring the existing `telephone` convention.\n- `PostcodeRange.java` (new model) \u2014 the pinned region\u2192range table (NSW 2000\u20112099, VIC 3000\u20113099, QLD 4000\u20114099), reusing `Locality.forCity(...)` for the city\u2192region lookup; unknown region accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n- Added the `postcode` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Request handling (OfficeFloor functions)**\n- `RequirePostcodeInRegion.java` (new step) \u2014 validates *only when present*: rejects malformed (not 4 digits) or out-of-range postcodes with 400; absent postcode passes through, keeping the contract backward-compatible.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML \u2014 checked exception \u2192 400 ProblemDetail, following the existing escalation pattern.\n- Wired `requirePostcode` into both `owners.POST.yml` (after required-fields) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (after validate).\n- `ApplyOwner.java` \u2014 now copies `postcode` on update; MapStruct auto-maps it by name for create and response.\n\nWhy the format check lives in the function rather than relying on DTO bean-validation: the POST pipeline binds `@RequestBody` without `@Valid`, so the DTO's `@Pattern` isn't enforced there (a malformed value otherwise reached the entity and failed at flush as a 500). The function now guarantees a 400 for both malformed and out-of-range cases.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
